practical:
  - label: Parking
    body: Street parking along Second Avenue and lot parking serving the Old Town block and Cottonwood Square. Free at time of writing; posted restrictions apply.
  - label: On foot
    body: Old Town is walkable end to end in about ten minutes, with continuous sidewalks and short crossings.
  - label: By bike
    body: The Longmont-to-Boulder (LoBo) Regional Trail runs through Niwot and connects to quiet county roads. The county’s trail page carries the map.
  - label: Transit
    body: RTD’s Route BOLT runs between Boulder and Longmont along the Diagonal, with a stop at Highway 119 and Niwot Road. Construction of the CO 119 bus rapid transit line has been changing stops on this corridor, so check the route page before traveling.
  - label: Dogs
    body: Leash and waste rules on trails and open space are set by Boulder County Parks & Open Space.
  - label: Best time
    body: Weekday mornings for a quiet walk. Summer Thursday evenings for the concert series beside the caboose.
